Environment note
----------------
The full `python build.py` run was attempted first, but this host has no cargo,
go, make, cmake, javac, ruby, luac, or ghc, and the npm launcher is not visible
to Windows CreateProcess. The source change is Python-only, so the focused
unittest suite above is the relevant validation. The diagnostic bundle was
generated with `python build.py -m backend` so build.py would still emit its
artifacts.

Encryptly note
--------------
The bundled tools/encryptly/windows-x64/encryptly.exe prints a generated
password and exits 1 without writing an archive on this host, so this .logd is
the plain-text build log. The companion JSON records the same limitation.
